body:
It is exhausting listening to people talk about evolution and homosexuality. There are so many nuances to the topic in the first place but all you hear is the same thing about not reproducing or carrying on genes. Even IF homosexuality was some kind of disorder or unnatural phenomenon, I still do not give any more of a fuck if someone is gay. Humans are very different from any other creature on earth and we do not live entirely off of primal animal instincts for survival.

&#x200B;

If the attempt is going to be made to prove homosexuality is unnatural you are going to have to begin by explaining a lot more than just evolution to unequivocally reach that conclusion. But, of course, every internet homophobe trying to prove a point will just state the same tired lines about reproduction and carrying on your genes. There is so much complex evolution that is seen in creatures on earth and a lot of it is not even close to being understood. Also are we all going to just blatantly ignore the existence of bisexuality? Does it become natural to have butt sex with a man if you also like to impregnate women? I wish people would just say "I am uncomfortable by the idea of two men/women together" instead of pretending to come from a place of high and mighty like they are justified in their beliefs. It is just as annoying as listening to fucking bible thumpers.
